hi ramasubbareddy,
		there are 5 sections. the cts people are having around 3 sets of papers which they will be changing all time from college to college. this is the toughest of all. I will be sending the remaining papers also. This paper will be marked as ctsiitk. O.K good luck.

Section-1
^^^^^^^^^

A(S,T)=	S		  IF T=(a) and a is not a member of S;
      = ST		  IF T=()  and a is a member of S;
      = Subtract S from T IF T=(a) and a is not a member of S;
      = ()		  other wise.


B(S,T)=S		  IF T=() and a is not a member of S;
      =T		  IF T=(a) and a is a member of S;
      =Subtract S from T  IF T=(a) and a is not a member of S;
      =()	          other wise.

S={a,b,(a,b),(b,b)},T={a,b,(a,a),(b,a)},U={b,(a,a),(b,a),(b,b)}.
      ( The above conditions are not fully correct.But the question is same)

Q.1.
A(S,T)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.2.
A(T,S)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.3.
A(S,S)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.4.
A(S,U)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.5.
B(T,U)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.6.
B(U,S)=
(a).       (b).		(c).		(d)
Q.7,Q.8 are also like this.


Section-2

note: here what u have to do is to identify the function and thats it u can solve the remaining questions easily.

^^^^^^^^^
This section is related to functions
Q.9

f(x)=f(1/x);
f(6)+f(15)=
(a)21 7/30 (b)12 4/30 (c)21 21/31 (d)20 5/31
[Here the actual function is f(x)= x + 1/x]

Q.10
f(x)=f(-1/x);
f(6)+f(15)=
(a)	(b)	(c)	(d)
[Here the actual function is f(x)= x - 1/x]

Q.11
f(x)=f(1/x);
f(6)+f(15)
(a)	(b)	(c)	(d)
[Here the actual function is f(x)= x*x + 1/(x*x)]

Q.12
f(x)=f(-1/x);
f(9)+f(15)=
(a)	(b)	(c)	(d)
[Here the function is f(x)=f(-1/x)]

